        skos:definition        "A device for measuring sea-surface waves. It consists of a surface buoy containing either a single accelerometer (measures non-directional wave height and period), an accelerometer plus compass or multiple accelerometers (latter two measure directional wave parameters) tethered to the seabed by an elastic rope. Deployed on a package of instruments or sensors as the second sensor of this type."@en;
